{title: Jesus Died In My Place}
{artist: Larry Holder / Elton Smith}
{time: 4/4}
{key: E}
{tempo: 129}

>Lyrics

(Short introduction)

Verse 1

There I stood condemned to die

For the sin that I had done,

With the gavel of the Judge soon to fall.

Jesus took my place instead,

For my sinful soul he bled,

There upon the cross He gladly paid it all!

Chorus

Jesus died in my place,

He was nailed by the hands of men

And hung there in disgrace.

Jesus died for my sin,

Now reborn by His loving grace,

I gladly give my life to Him.

Verse 2

As He hung upon the cross

Bearing all the weight of sin,

Jesus blessed the hands that nailed Him to the tree.

Looking far beyond His loss

To the crown that He would win,

And the home he would

prepare for you and me.

(Repeat Chorus)

Jesus died in my place,

He was nailed by the hands of men

And hung there in disgrace.

Jesus died for my sin,

Now reborn by His loving grace,

I gladly give my life to Him.

Bridge

And as His blood was falling,

To the earth His life descending,

His love was reaching to me,

Cleansing me from sin.

(Repeat Chorus)

Jesus died in my place,

He was nailed by the hands of men

And hung there in disgrace.

Jesus died for my sin,

Now reborn by His loving grace,

I gladly give my life to Him.

(Raise Key and Repeat Chorus)

Jesus died in my place,

He was nailed by the hands of men

And hung there in disgrace.

Jesus died for my sin,

Now reborn by His loving grace,

I gladly give my life to Him.
